# Coding Standards

## Conditional classes — use `cn` with object syntax

Never use ternary or `&&` inside `cn()`. Use object keys for conditional classes.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
cn("base", isActive && "text-primary", isRTL ? "left-8" : "right-8")

// ✅ GOOD
cn("base", { "text-primary": isActive, "left-8": isRTL, "right-8": !isRTL })
```

## Conditional rendering — use ternary, not `&&`

Use `? :` for JSX conditionals. Avoid nested ternaries.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
{footer && <Footer />}
{icon && <Icon />}

// ✅ GOOD
{footer ? <Footer /> : null}
{icon ? <Icon /> : null}
```

## ENUMs over hardcoded strings

```ts
export enum USER_ROLE {
  ADMIN = "ADMIN",
  USER = "USER",
}
```

## Colors — theme tokens only

Never use hardcoded colors (`bg-[#898989]`, `bg-gray-500`, `bg-slate-900`). Use defined CSS tokens (`bg-primary`, `bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`).

## Sizing — prefer `size-*`

Use `size-5` instead of `h-5 w-5`.

## Routes — use route enums/constants

Never hardcode route strings. Use route objects/enums from `constants/endpoints.ts`:

```tsx
router.push(FRONTEND_ROUTES.STUDENT_CURRICULUMS)
```

## shadcn/ui — wrap, don't modify

Do not edit `components/ui/*` shadcn primitives. Create App wrappers (e.g. `AppInput`, `AppButton`) and customize there.

## Spacing & CSS hygiene

- No negative margin or padding (`-m-*`, `-p-*`)
- No `!` important overrides (`text-sm!`)
- No arbitrary values (`p-[30px]`) — use Tailwind scale tokens

## i18n

Keep user-facing text in locale files (e.g. `en.json`). No hardcoded UI copy in components when adding new features.

## Components

Prefer reusable, focused components. Keep pages thin; extract shared UI (headers, footers, links, buttons).

- Use `AppState` / `AppQueryState` for loading, empty, and error UI
- Use `AppSkeleton` for list placeholders
- Use `DashboardShell` for student/admin layouts — do not duplicate sidebar/header logic
- Use `ConfirmationModal` with `variant="danger"` instead of bespoke delete modals

## Imports — no unused barrel files

Do not add feature-level `index.ts` re-export barrels unless something actually imports from that path.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — unused index.ts that re-exports everything
export * from "./hooks";

// ✅ GOOD — import from the concrete module
import { useStudentCurriculums } from "@/hooks/student/useStudentCurriculums";
```

## API layer — React Query required for client data fetching

- **Never** call `apiInstance` directly inside page `useEffect` for new features
- Use typed helpers from `lib/api/api-client.ts`
- Use endpoint constants from `constants/endpoints.ts` — never hardcode API paths
- Define query keys in `lib/api/query-keys.ts`
- Put domain hooks in `hooks/<domain>/` (e.g. `hooks/student/useStudentCurriculums.ts`)

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
export function useStudentCurriculums() {
  return useApiQuery({
    queryKey: queryKeys.student.curriculums(),
    queryFn: () => apiGet<Curriculum[]>(API_ENDPOINTS.STUDENT.CURRICULUM),
  });
}
```

## Mutations

Use `useApiMutation` with `invalidateKeys` for cache updates after create/update/delete.

## Pages

Pages should orchestrate hooks + presentational components. No fetch logic in JSX.

## Types

- API responses: `ApiSuccessResponse<T>` from `types/api.ts`
- Avoid `as any` on API responses — type the `data` generic
